    "goal": "Materialize a breadth-adequate, non-outcome-exposed replacement scope for the BREAKOUT_VOLATILITY_EXPANSION/FADE family (successor design to the breadth-insufficient V2-C032 identity) by intersecting already-accepted, reusable structural evidence — the 40-symbol frontier univariate structural gate, breakout event availability, 15M directional follow-through, 30M directional persistence, and the pre-economic realizability audit — with the EUR200 margin feasibility index, so the next economic-eligible candidate carries enough structurally heterogeneous symbols to clear the breadth gate that C032 failed on.",
    "information_gain_rationale": "C032 was rejected as BREADTH_INSUFFICIENT_FOR_SCOPE_CHARGED (1 symbol) despite a mechanism family with the richest existing non-economic evidence stack in the eligibility packet (event availability + two independent directional-persistence horizons + a pre-economic realizability audit + a fresh pooled serial-dependence screen across 40 series showing consistent negative autocorrelation at h=1,3,6). Reassembling breadth from these already-accepted artifacts, rather than proposing a new mechanism from scratch, maximizes information gain per unit of scarce economic capacity: it reuses fully-vetted structural evidence, respects the causal prohibition on rerunning C032's opened identity, and produces the smallest remaining gap (fresh cost/margin/exact-head confirmation) before an economic freeze can be legally authorized."
  },
